<title>FRANCE: French households less pessimistic in October.</title>
<headline>French households less pessimistic in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>INSEE gave the following data on household opinions. A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying things had worsened.</p>
<p>				     Oct  Sept  July Jun  May  Apr  Mar</p>
<p> Overall confidence index    -34  -37  -35  -36  -38  -35  -33</p>
<p> Past living standards	 -72  -73  -73  -72  -71  -70  -64</p>
<p> Future living standards     -38  -45  -45  -44  -44  -40  -35</p>
<p> Future unemployment	    72   79   77   60   67   67   66</p>
<p> Past inflation		  -51  -54  -47  -42  -41  -38  -40</p>
<p> Future inflation		-36  -37  -44  -40  -36  -34  -35</p>
<p> Good time to spend	    -31  -35  -32  -32  -30  -28  -29</p>
<p> Good time to save		55   52   50   56   49   47   45</p>
<p> Current personal finances     6   10    9   10    7    8    5</p>
<p> Past personal finances	-23  -23  -23  -25  -25  -24  -24</p>
<p> Future personal finances     -8  -11  -10  -10  -13  -10   -9</p>
<p> Ability to save		 -29  -32  -30  -30  -31  -32  -33</p>
